<!-- **The SQL half of SnippetVeil, loaded only where the database plugin is.**

     `plugin.xml` declares `com.intellij.database` as an optional dependency naming this file, so what
     is registered here is present exactly when Database Tools and SQL is installed and enabled — which
     is also exactly when anything can inject SQL into a literal. Everywhere else a SQL string is one
     redacted literal, and nothing says so: which plugins an IDE has is not something the output may
     tell anyone.

     **The boundary is a JVM one**, as it is for Kotlin. The class named below links against
     `com.intellij.sql.*` and `com.intellij.database.*`, so it is loaded only from here, and no class
     reachable from the main descriptor may name those types. `ShippedCodeArchitectureTest` asserts that
     over shipped bytecode and demonstrates it red. -->
<idea-plugin>
    <extensions defaultExtensionNs="com.snippetveil">
        <injectedContainer implementation="com.snippetveil.plugin.sql.SqlContainer"/>
    </extensions>
</idea-plugin>
